# 
# --- Constr_ClientServer_StaticCorrectness_Rationale (信息性) ---
# id: Constr_ClientServer_StaticCorrectness_Rationale
# title: Rationale for Client/Server Compatibility (Static Correctness)
# expression: A client shall call a certain operation to allow the server to work correctly (in the context of static correctness for Client/Server compatibility).
# 

# 
# --- Constr_ComSpec_Optionality (信息性) ---
# id: Constr_ComSpec_Optionality
# title: ComSpec Optionality
# expression: The communication specification is optional, i.e. its existence is not required in any case.
# 

# 
# --- Constr_ComSpec_PortInterface_Typing (信息性) ---
# id: Constr_ComSpec_PortInterface_Typing
# title: ComSpec Subclass and PortInterface Typing
# expression: Specific subclasses of ComSpec can only be owned by PortPrototypes typed by the corresponding kind of PortInterface.
# 

# 
# --- Constr_ComSpec_Usage_Scope (信息性) ---
# id: Constr_ComSpec_Usage_Scope
# title: ComSpec Usage Scope
# expression: The usage of ComSpecs is not restricted to the PortPrototypes of AtomicSwComponentTypes.
# 

# 
# --- Constr_CompositionSwCT_DataTypeMappingCapability ---
# 
ex:Shape_Constr_CompositionSwCT_DataTypeMappingCapability a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass autosar:COMPOSITION-SW-COMPONENT-TYPE ;
    sh:message "DataType and ConstantValue Mapping Capability for CompositionSwComponentType — It shall be possible to define mappings of ApplicationDataTypes..." ;
    sh:severity sh:Violation ;
    sh:property
        [
            a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:path ( autosar:CONSTANT-VALUE-MAPPING-REFS autosar:CONSTANT-VALUE-MAPPING-REF ) ;
            # maxOccurs = -1
            sh:class autosar:CONSTANT-SPECIFICATION-MAPPING-SET ; # from ref_dest_literals
        ],
        [
            a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:path ( autosar:DATA-TYPE-MAPPING-REFS autosar:DATA-TYPE-MAPPING-REF ) ;
            # maxOccurs = -1
            sh:class autosar:DATA-TYPE-MAPPING-SET ; # from ref_dest_literals
        ]
    .

# 
# --- Constr_CompositionSwCType_No_VFB_Effect_No_New_Functionality (信息性) ---
# id: Constr_CompositionSwCType_No_VFB_Effect_No_New_Functionality
# title: CompositionSwComponentTypes effect on VFB and functionality
# expression: the deﬁnition of CompositionSwComponentTypes has no effect on how software-components interact with the Virtual Functional Bus (VFB). CompositionSwComponentTypes do not add any new functionality to what is already provided by the software-components they aggregate.
# 

# 
